## API Reference

### Complete Endpoint Documentation

#### Authentication Endpoints

**`POST /api/v1/auth/challenge`**
- **Auth:** None
- **Rate Limit:** 15 req/min per IP (fixed window)
- **Request:**
  ```json
  {
    "chainId": "solana-mainnet",
    "walletAddress": "7xKz...9Qp",
    "audience": "your-app-id"  // optional
  }
  ```
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "message": "{\"chain\":\"solana-mainnet\",\"address\":\"7xkz...9qp\",\"iat\":1699564800,\"exp\":1699565100,\"nonce\":\"abc123...\",\"aud\":\"your-app-id\"}",
    "chainId": "solana-mainnet",
    "address": "7xkz...9qp",
    "issuedAt": 1699564800,
    "expiresAt": 1699565100,
    "nonce": "abc123...",
    "audience": "your-app-id",
    "mac": "def456...",
    "mkv": "v1"
  }
  ```
- **Errors:** 400 (invalid params), 422 (business rule), 429 (rate limit), 500 (server error)

---

**`POST /api/v1/auth/verify`**
- **Auth:** None
- **Rate Limit:** ⚠️ **Not Configured** (endpoint references "AuthVerify" policy but policy not found in configuration)
- **Request:**
  ```json
  {
    "chainId": "solana-mainnet",
    "address": "7xkz...9qp",
    "signedMessage": "{\"chain\":\"solana-mainnet\",...}",
    "signature": "base58-encoded-signature",
    "mac": "def456...",
    "mkv": "v1"
  }
  ```
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
    "tokenType": "Bearer",
    "expiresIn": 900,  // 15 minutes in seconds
    "axonUserId": "uuid-here",
    "created": true,  // true if new user
    "walletsLinked": 1,
    "conflicts": 0
  }
  ```
- **Errors:** 400 (expired challenge, invalid), 401 (invalid signature/MAC), 409 (replay/conflict), 422 (business rule), 429 (rate limit), 500 (server error)

---

**`POST /api/v1/auth/exchange`**
- **Auth:** None (but requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header)
- **Rate Limit:** 10 req/min per IP (fixed window)
- **Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <Dynamic JWT OR Axon Access Token>`
- **Request Body:** `{ "placeholder": null }` (body ignored, token from header)
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
    "tokenType": "Bearer",
    "expiresIn": 900,
    "axonUserId": "uuid-here",
    "created": false,
    "walletsLinked": 3,
    "conflicts": 0
  }
  ```
- **Behavior:** Validates bearer token (Dynamic JWT or Axon token), creates/updates principal, links wallets, issues new Axon token
- **Errors:** 400 (malformed token), 401 (invalid/expired token), 409 (wallet conflict), 422 (business rule), 429 (rate limit), 500 (server error)

---

**`POST /api/v1/auth/refresh`**
- **Auth:** None (requires refresh token in body)
- **Rate Limit:** 10 req/min per IP (fixed window)
- **Request:**
  ```json
  {
    "refreshToken": "refresh-token-string-here"
  }
  ```
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "accessToken": "new-access-token",
    "refreshToken": "new-refresh-token",
    "tokenType": "Bearer",
    "expiresIn": 900,
    "issuedAt": "2025-10-07T12:00:00Z",
    "accessTokenExpiresAt": "2025-10-07T12:15:00Z",
    "refreshTokenExpiresAt": "2025-11-06T12:00:00Z"
  }
  ```
- **Behavior:** Validates refresh token, generates new access+refresh tokens, **revokes old refresh token** (token rotation)
- **Errors:** 400 (invalid request), 401 (invalid/expired refresh token), 429 (rate limit), 500 (server error)

---

**`GET /api/v1/auth/me`**
- **Auth:** Required (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
- **Rate Limit:** 10 req/min per IP (uses "AuthExchange" policy)
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "profile": {
      "axonId": "uuid-here",
      "riskTier": "Low"  // Low | Medium | High
    },
    "wallets": [
      {
        "chain": "solana",
        "address": "7xkz...9qp",
        "state": "Verified",  // Pending | Verified | Revoked
        "access": "Signing",  // Signing | WatchOnly
        "isDefault": true
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
- **Errors:** 401 (not authenticated), 403 (forbidden), 500 (server error)

---

#### Chat Endpoints

**`POST /api/v1/chat/turns`**
- **Auth:** Required (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
- **Rate Limit:** 100 req/min per IP (global default policy)
- **Request:**
  ```json
  {
    "conversationId": "uuid-or-null",  // null = start new
    "message": "Your message here (1-32K chars)"
  }
  ```
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "conversationId": "uuid-here",
    "userMessageId": "uuid-here",
    "assistantMessageId": "uuid-here",
    "assistantMessage": "AI response content here",
    "timestamp": "2025-10-07T12:00:00Z"
  }
  ```
- **Behavior:** If conversationId null → start new conversation, else append to existing. Persists user message, calls AI, persists assistant message, returns response.
- **Business Rules:** Max 100 messages per conversation, turn-taking enforced (User → Assistant alternation)
- **Errors:** 400 (invalid params), 401 (not authenticated), 403 (forbidden), 422 (business rule violated), 500 (server error)

---

**`GET /api/v1/chat/conversations`**
- **Auth:** Required (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
- **Rate Limit:** 100 req/min per IP (global default policy)
- **Query Params:**
  - `pageSize` (default: 20, max: 100)
  - `pageNumber` (default: 1, 1-indexed)
  - `sortBy` (default: "UpdatedAt", options: "UpdatedAt" | "CreatedAt")
  - `sortDirection` (default: "desc", options: "desc" | "asc")
  - `titleContains` (optional search filter)
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "conversationId": "uuid-here",
        "title": "Conversation about Solana staking",
        "createdAt": "2025-10-07T12:00:00Z",
        "updatedAt": "2025-10-07T12:30:00Z",
        "lastAssistantResponseId": "uuid-or-null"
      }
    ],
    "pageNumber": 1,
    "pageSize": 20,
    "totalCount": 47,
    "totalPages": 3,
    "hasNext": true,
    "hasPrevious": false,
    "count": 20,
    "isEmpty": false,
    "firstItemIndex": 1,
    "lastItemIndex": 20
  }
  ```
- **Errors:** 400 (invalid params), 401 (not authenticated), 403 (forbidden), 500 (server error)

---

**`GET /api/v1/chat/conversations/{conversationId}/messages`**
- **Auth:** Required (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
- **Rate Limit:** 100 req/min per IP (global default policy)
- **Path Param:** `conversationId` (UUID)
- **Query Params:**
  - `pageSize` (default: 50, max: 100)
  - `pageNumber` (default: 1, 1-indexed)
  - `includeDeleted` (default: false)
- **Response (200):**
  ```json
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "messageId": "uuid-here",
        "role": "user",  // "user" | "assistant"
        "content": "Message content here",
        "createdAt": "2025-10-07T12:00:00Z",
        "sequence": 1,
        "aiResponseId": null  // Only for assistant messages
      }
    ],
    "pageNumber": 1,
    "pageSize": 50,
    "totalCount": 12,
    "totalPages": 1,
    "hasNext": false,
    "hasPrevious": false,
    "count": 12,
    "isEmpty": false,
    "firstItemIndex": 1,
    "lastItemIndex": 12
  }
  ```
- **Errors:** 400 (invalid params), 401 (not authenticated), 403 (forbidden, not owner), 404 (conversation not found), 500 (server error)

---

### Rate Limits & Quotas

| Endpoint | Rate Limit | Notes |
|----------|------------|-------|
| `/auth/challenge` | 15 req/min per IP | `AuthChallenge` policy |
| `/auth/verify` | ⚠️ **Not Configured** | Backend issue: policy undefined |
| `/auth/exchange` | 10 req/min per IP | `AuthExchange` policy |
| `/chat/*` | 100 req/min per IP | Global default |

**Token TTLs:** Challenge: 5 min | Access: 15 min | Refresh: 30 days
**Message Limits:** 1-32K chars | 100 messages/conversation
**SDK Handling:** Auto-retry with exponential backoff (1s → 2s → 4s) | Respects `Retry-After` header

---

## Integration Patterns

### Pattern 1: Embedded Widget (Vanilla JS - Any Site)

**Use Case:** Add AI chat to WordPress, Webflow, static HTML, or any site without build tools.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>My Website</title>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Your website content -->
  <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
  <p>Content here...</p>

  <!-- Axon Chat Widget (add before </body>) -->
  <script src="https://cdn.axon.ai/chat-widget.js" async></script>
  <axon-chat-bubble
    environment-id="axon-mainnet"
    auth-mode="dynamic"
    dynamic-environment-id="YOUR_DYNAMIC_ID"
    theme="auto"
    position="bottom-right"
    greeting-message="👋 Hi! I'm your AI assistant. Ask me anything!"
  />
</body>
</html>
```

**Configuration via Attributes:**

```html
<axon-chat-bubble
  <!-- Required -->
  environment-id="axon-mainnet"
  auth-mode="dynamic"

  <!-- Dynamic.xyz (if auth-mode="dynamic") -->
  dynamic-environment-id="YOUR_DYNAMIC_ID"

  <!-- OR Wallet Adapter (if auth-mode="wallet") -->
  wallet-provider="phantom"  <!-- phantom | solflare | backpack -->

  <!-- Appearance -->
  theme="dark"  <!-- dark | light | auto -->
  primary-color="#7C3AED"
  position="bottom-right"  <!-- bottom-right | bottom-left | top-right | top-left -->

  <!-- Content -->
  greeting-message="👋 Hi! Ask me anything!"
  placeholder="Type your message..."
  empty-state-message="No conversations yet"

  <!-- Behavior -->
  auto-open="false"
  default-conversation-id=""  <!-- Resume specific conversation -->
/>
```

**Browser Support:**
- ✅ Chrome 90+
- ✅ Firefox 88+
- ✅ Safari 14+
- ✅ Edge 90+
- ⚠️ IE 11 (fallback to iframe mode)

---

### Pattern 2: React App with Dynamic.xyz

**Use Case:** React app using Dynamic.xyz for wallet authentication.

**Installation:**

```bash
npm install @axon-ai/sdk-react @axon-ai/sdk-chat-ui @dynamic-labs/sdk-react-core @dynamic-labs/ethereum
```

**Implementation:**

```typescript
// app.tsx
import { DynamicContextProvider, useDynamicContext } from '@dynamic-labs/sdk-react-core';
import { EthereumWalletConnectors } from '@dynamic-labs/ethereum';
import { AxonProvider, AxonChatBubble } from '@axon-ai/sdk-react';

function App() {
  return (
    <DynamicContextProvider
      settings={{
        environmentId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_DYNAMIC_ENVIRONMENT_ID!,
        walletConnectors: [EthereumWalletConnectors],
        eventsCallbacks: {
          onAuthSuccess: (args) => {
            console.log('Dynamic auth success:', args.user);
          },
        },
      }}
    >
      <AppContent />
    </DynamicContextProvider>
  );
}

function AppContent() {
  const { authToken, user, isAuthenticated } = useDynamicContext();

  return (
    <AxonProvider
      config={{
        environment: 'mainnet',
        authMode: 'dynamic',
        dynamicToken: authToken,  // Auto-exchange when token changes
        onAuthSuccess: (userId) => {
          console.log('Axon auth success:', userId);
        },
        onError: (error) => {
          console.error('Axon error:', error);
        },
      }}
    >
      <main>
        <h1>My dApp</h1>
        {isAuthenticated ? (
          <p>Welcome, {user?.email ?? user?.walletPublicKey}!</p>
        ) : (
          <p>Please connect your wallet to continue</p>
        )}

        {/* Your app content */}
      </main>

      {/* Chat bubble (only renders when authenticated) */}
      <AxonChatBubble
        position="bottom-right"
        theme={{
          colors: {
            primary: '#7C3AED',
            background: '#1F2937',
          },
          typography: {
            fontFamily: 'Geist, system-ui',
          },
        }}
        onConversationStart={(id) => {
          console.log('Conversation started:', id);
        }}
      />
    </AxonProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

**Environment Variables (.env.local):**

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_DYNAMIC_ENVIRONMENT_ID=your-dynamic-environment-id
```

---

## Developer Experience

### TypeScript Support

**Full Type Coverage:**

```typescript
// All SDK types are fully typed
import type {
  AxonClient,
  AuthTokenResponse,
  ChallengeResponse,
  ChatTurnRequest,
  ChatTurnResponse,
  Conversation,
  Message,
  User,
  AxonTheme,
  AxonConfig,
} from '@axon-ai/sdk-core';

// React hooks are fully typed
import { useAxonAuth, useConversation } from '@axon-ai/sdk-react';

const auth = useAxonAuth();
//    ^? { isAuthenticated: boolean; user: User | null; signIn: () => Promise<void>; ... }

const chat = useConversation(conversationId);
//    ^? { messages: Message[]; sendMessage: (text: string) => Promise<ChatTurnResponse>; ... }
```

