### Plugin System (Advanced Usage)

**Extensibility Without Forking**

The SDK supports a plugin system for extending behavior without modifying core code.

**Plugin Interface:**

```typescript
interface AxonPlugin {
  name: string;
  version?: string;

  // Lifecycle hooks
  onInit?: (client: AxonClient) => void | Promise<void>;
  onRequest?: (request: RequestContext) => RequestContext | Promise<RequestContext>;
  onResponse?: (response: ResponseContext) => ResponseContext | Promise<ResponseContext>;
  onError?: (error: ErrorContext) => void | Promise<void>;
  onDestroy?: () => void | Promise<void>;
}

interface RequestContext {
  url: string;
  method: string;
  headers: Headers;
  body?: any;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
}

interface ResponseContext {
  status: number;
  headers: Headers;
  body: any;
  duration: number;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
}

interface ErrorContext {
  error: Error;
  request: RequestContext;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
}
```

**Built-In Plugins:**

```typescript
import {
  retryPlugin,
  rateLimitPlugin,
  analyticsPlugin,
  cachePlugin
} from '@axon-ai/sdk-core/plugins';

const axon = new AxonClient({
  environment: 'mainnet',
  plugins: [
    // Retry failed requests with exponential backoff
    retryPlugin({
      maxRetries: 3,
      retryableStatusCodes: [408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504],
      backoffMultiplier: 2
    }),

    // Client-side rate limiting (prevent hitting backend limits)
    rateLimitPlugin({
      maxRequestsPerMinute: 60,
      strategy: 'sliding-window'
    }),

    // Track usage analytics
    analyticsPlugin({
      track: (event, data) => {
        mixpanel.track(event, data);
      }
    }),

    // Client-side caching (complementary to TanStack Query)
    cachePlugin({
      ttl: 60_000, // 1 minute
      maxSize: 100 // entries
    })
  ]
});
```

**Custom Plugin Example:**

```typescript
// Request signing plugin
const requestSigningPlugin: AxonPlugin = {
  name: 'request-signing',
  version: '1.0.0',

  async onRequest(ctx) {
    // Sign requests with custom signature
    const timestamp = Date.now();
    const signature = await signRequest(ctx.body, timestamp, SECRET_KEY);

    return {
      ...ctx,
      headers: {
        ...ctx.headers,
        'X-Signature': signature,
        'X-Timestamp': timestamp.toString()
      }
    };
  },

  async onResponse(ctx) {
    // Verify response signature
    const serverSignature = ctx.headers.get('X-Server-Signature');
    const isValid = await verifyResponse(ctx.body, serverSignature);

    if (!isValid) {
      throw new Error('Invalid server signature');
    }

    return ctx;
  }
};

const axon = new AxonClient({
  environment: 'mainnet',
  plugins: [requestSigningPlugin]
});
```

**Multi-Chain Preparation Plugin:**

```typescript
// Plugin for multi-chain wallet support (future)
const multiChainPlugin: AxonPlugin = {
  name: 'multi-chain',

  async onRequest(ctx) {
    // Automatically detect chain from wallet address
    const walletAddress = ctx.metadata.walletAddress;
    const chain = detectChain(walletAddress);

    return {
      ...ctx,
      headers: {
        ...ctx.headers,
        'X-Chain-Type': chain // 'solana' | 'ethereum' | 'cosmos'
      }
    };
  }
};
```

**Benefits:**
- ✅ **Extensible**: Add custom behavior without forking SDK
- ✅ **Composable**: Mix and match plugins
- ✅ **Reusable**: Share plugins across projects
- ✅ **Type-Safe**: Full TypeScript support

